course: dictionary
lesson: 8018
title: Referral: being sent on for help
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A referral is when someone sends you to another person or place that can help you better. The example says, «A food bank is a charity that gives free food parcels, usually after a referral from someone like a school or a doctor.» The school or doctor does not give the food. They send the family on to the food bank.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «From someone like a school or a doctor» tells you who does the sending. The word «after» tells you the referral comes first, and the food parcels come later. Try your meaning in the sentence: "usually after being sent on for help from someone like a school or a doctor". It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Referral can also mean the letter or note that does the sending, as in «referral letter». Many words have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one is meant. If you are still unsure, check a dictionary.
fact: A referral is the act of sending someone to another person or place that can help them better.
fact: In health, a family doctor often makes a referral to a specialist at a hospital.
fact: A referral can also be the letter or note that sends someone on.
fact: In shops and apps, a referral can be when a customer recommends a shop to a friend, sometimes for a reward.
fact: Useful phrases: «get a referral», «referral letter», «self-referral».
exercise: «A food bank is a charity that gives free food parcels, usually after a referral from someone like a school or a doctor.» Who usually makes the referral in this sentence? | The family's pet | A shop with a reward scheme | *A school or a doctor | Food bank workers
exercise: What is a referral from a family doctor usually? | A test you pass at school | A bill for a visit | A holiday abroad | *Being sent to a specialist who can help you better
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that names a letter that sends someone on for help. | food bank | *referral letter | free parcels | charity
test: «The teacher made a referral to the school nurse.» What does referral mean here? | *Sending the child to someone who can help | Writing the child's name on the register | Telling the child off | Giving the child a sweet
test: When a customer tells a friend about a shop and gets a reward, what is this called? | A receipt | A rebate | A refund | *A referral
exam: «Mia's doctor gave her a referral to a hospital specialist.» Why did the doctor make a referral? | To test Mia's eyes at school | To give Mia a holiday | To stop Mia coming back to the surgery | *So a specialist could help Mia better
